# What must not reach a build context rooted here.
#
# Only builds whose context is the repo root read this file — `apps/rapi` builds
# from its own directory and is unaffected.

# **The one that bit.** Without this, `COPY apps/pwa apps/pwa` carries the
# developer's `.env` into the image, and Vite reads it: a production bundle went
# out pointing at `http://127.0.0.1:3000`. It builds, it deploys, it serves, and
# every request goes to a machine that is not there.
#
# The values a build needs arrive as build arguments. A file that sets the same
# names is a second source of truth that only the person who has it can see.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile, and a host `node_modules` is
# built for the host's platform.
**/node_modules

# The image builds this itself. A stale local copy would be shipped instead of
# the one the build just produced.
**/dist
**/dev-dist

.git
**/.turbo
**/tmp
**/log
**/*.log
